From c95919886b9eccba1ad375a15985e5aae2735384 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: starbite <starbite@local>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:21:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] patch: 0426-starbite-m5-power-drivers.patch - StarbiteACPM,
 StarbiteRTC, StarbiteWatchdog, StarbiteBattery built in for STARLTE (copies
 of starbite/apple-drivers at 4a7ec17 under iokit/Kernel/arm/starbite,
 STARLTE-only build units), matched on the board ADT's acpm-ipc / wdt-cl1 /
 hsi2c-pmic nodes; SweetWatchdog.cpp off on STARLTE (StarbiteWatchdog defines
 IOWatchdog), the IOResources IOWatchdog and SweetBattery wait for
 StarbiteLegacyBoard, which the platform expert publishes only without board
 nodes, so today's ADTs boot as before; starlte_touch.c's ACPM client steps
 aside for StarbiteACPM when the ADT has acpm-ipc (PMIC/DVFS calls routed
 through it, hazard H1); the platform expert takes the time of day from
 StarbiteRTC; sbstop test boots skip the root search (sbstoproot=1 to search);
 sbstop=m5 waits up to 50 s for the four drivers, prints a summary and stops

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
